Introduced by #34263 . `sessionVars.TxnCtx` gets initialized [here](https://github.com/pingcap/tidb/pull/34263/files?diff=split&w=0#diff-10dab83c04a99358d431906d37f48b92be97d50a2719d4ddf81c62d3b03a0aebR3151), In this case, it's 'temptable.AttachLocalTemporaryTableInfoSchema(p.Sctx, domain.GetDomain(p.Sctx).InfoSchema()) -> **domain.InfoSchema()**' now, rather than previous 'session.GetInfoSchema() -> **sessionVars.SnapshotInfoschema**'.

Dumpling will execute `SHOW TABLE STATUS FROM ...`, the show stmt triggers a [restricted sql](https://github.com/pingcap/tidb/blob/53f228af451e8b347d60e68a82a5bf9978692c16/executor/show.go#L535-L541) within the current session, as a result, `sessionVars.SnapshotInfoschema` is reset to nil [here](https://github.com/pingcap/tidb/blob/53f228af451e8b347d60e68a82a5bf9978692c16/session/session.go#L1739). After that, when we call `session.GetInfoSchema()`, `sessionVars.TxnCtx.InfoSchema` is returned instead of `sessionVars.SnapshotInfoschema`, thus `drop database` is visible after `SHOW TABLE STATUS FROM ...`. The schema version changed unexpectedly during transaction!

@cfzjywxk @lcwangchao PTAL

The minimal reproducible steps:
```sql
/* test */ use test;
/* test */ drop table if exists t;
/* test */ do sleep(1);
/* test */ do @t := now();
/* test */ create table t (a int);
/* test */ show tables;

/* test */ set tidb_snapshot = @t;
/* test */ show tables; -- empty
/* test */ show table status from test;
/* test */ show tables; -- [t]

/* test */ set tidb_snapshot = @t;
/* test */ start transaction with consistent snapshot;
/* test */ show tables; -- empty
/* test */ show table status from test;
/* test */ show tables; -- [t]
/* test */ rollback;
```
